cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.'
title: 'IELTS API: a free, open, no-authentication TypeScript API for IELTS band conversion, CEFR alignment and writing analytics'
abstract: >-
  IELTS API is a dependency-free, MIT licensed TypeScript service that exposes
  IELTS band score conversion, IELTS-to-CEFR alignment, deterministic
  readability and lexical analytics for written responses, and an openly
  licensed corpus of writing, speaking and reading practice material. The API
  requires no authentication, performs no network or model inference at request
  time, and is fully deterministic, which makes every result exactly
  reproducible from a pinned commit.
type: software
authors:
  - name: 'IELTS API Contributors'
version: '1.0.0'
date-released: '2026-09-04'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/johnlikescarrot/IELTS-API'
url: 'https://github.com/johnlikescarrot/IELTS-API'
keywords:
  - IELTS
  - language testing
  - CEFR
  - automated writing evaluation
  - readability
  - open science
  - reproducible research
  - TypeScript
  - REST API
